DESCRIPTION

Model-Based Systems Engineering environment for Software-Defined Vehicles, built
on WebGME. The lifecycle of an SDV (requirements, functional, logical and
physical architecture, subsystem design, implementation, testing, validation and
deployment) is captured as structured, versioned models that several engineers
can edit at the same time. It includes a metamodel for the SDV lifecycle and for
hierarchical finite state machines, an example project, a REST API and an MCP
server that exposes the model operations to LLM clients.


RELATED PUBLICATIONS

There are no publications specifically related to this software. The
methodology it implements is described in the public CODE4EV deliverable
D2.1 - SDV design methodology (https://code4ev.eu).


APIS

This software does not require access to third-party APIs.
The included MCP server can be used by LLM clients chosen by the user. Such
clients are external services for which the user shall bear sole
